<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API. Do not paste this back into
        <description>. NOTE ALSO: the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment
        placed ABOVE <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        DESCRIPTION TRIMMED 2026-08-09 - IT WAS 259 CHARACTERS AGAINST THE 255 CAP. Found by
        MEASURING every <description> in this tranche rather than eyeballing them, after the
        Disposition_NDA record type breached the same cap at 266. The fact cut from
        <description> is restated here: the two counts it reads are DERIVED by the
        NDA_Signed_Rollup flow, which is also why that flow must deploy BEFORE this rule.

        THE ALL-SIGNED RELEASE GATE. On an OFF-MARKET disposition, nothing is released to a
        prospective buyer until every NDA collected against that disposition reads Signed.
        Source: Part 2 line 305, "nothing is released until this is done".

        IT BLOCKS EVERY FORWARD STAGE FROM NDA ONWARD, NOT JUST THE NEXT HOP (decision D15/Q4).
        Disposition_Stage__c is freely settable - the No_Backward_Stage_Movement rule is
        Opportunity-only and nothing stops a user jumping NDA -> LOI directly. Gating only the
        NDA -> Disposition Offer hop would therefore be a gate a single click bypasses, so the
        rule names Disposition Offer, LOI, PSA, Closing AND Completed. A future off-market stage
        added after NDA must be added to this OR list explicitly; it is NOT covered
        automatically. Same maintenance contract as
        Opportunity.NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression, which carries the identical warning.

        WHY THE RECORD-TYPE TEST IS REQUIRED. Four of the five gated stages - LOI, PSA, Closing,
        Completed - are SHARED with the on-market path, where NDAs are not collected at all and
        this gate must never fire. Only Disposition Offer and NDA are off-market-only. So unlike
        a value-set-disjoint rule, this one cannot be self-limiting by stage value and needs an
        explicit record-type criterion.

        RECORD-TYPE SYNTAX - A DELIBERATE SUBSTITUTION, FLAGGED SO IT IS NOT READ AS DRIFT. The
        Tranche 3 design and the build brief both write $RecordType.DeveloperName. Salesforce's
        own guidance ("Tips for Referencing Record Types in Formulas") is to AVOID the
        $RecordType global in formulas except in default-value formulas, and to use the
        RecordType merge field instead. RecordType.DeveloperName is used below. It is the same
        scoping decision, expressed in the form the platform documents as supported. It is a
        NAME comparison, not an Id, so it survives an org rebuild - but it will break if the
        Off_Market record type is ever renamed, which is the accepted trade the same guidance
        describes.

        WHY ISCHANGED ONLY - DELIBERATELY DIVERGING FROM ITS SIBLING
        Wire_Complete_Before_Completed, which uses OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)). Tranche 3's own
        test surface creates off-market dispositions DIRECTLY at LOI and PSA to exercise the
        LOI and PSA features, and ISNEW() would block its own fixtures. DispositionService.
        findOrCreate is the only production creator and always creates at Disposition Readiness,
        so the create path is not a real exposure. THE RESIDUAL IS REAL AND IS ACCEPTED:
        creating a disposition directly at a later stage bypasses this gate entirely.

        WHY BLANKVALUE. NDA_Count__c and Signed_NDA_Count__c carry defaultValue 0, but a default
        applies only at INSERT - every Disposition__c row that existed before those fields were
        created holds NULL. A null Number in a comparison makes the whole expression null, which
        a validation rule treats as FALSE - so the naive form NDA_Count__c = 0 would FAIL OPEN on
        exactly the pre-existing rows, letting a disposition with no NDAs at all sail past the
        gate. BLANKVALUE(...,0) makes both terms total. Do not "simplify" it away.

        NDA_Count__c = 0 IS A BLOCKING CONDITION, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. A disposition on which NO NDA
        was ever collected must not advance: collecting nothing is not the same as collecting
        everything. That is also why the rollup maintains TWO counts rather than one unsigned
        count, which would read 0 in both situations.

        🔴 A DECLINED NDA NO LONGER BLOCKS - AMENDED 2026-08-09 BY DECISION D20/C2, AND THE
        FORMULA BELOW DID NOT CHANGE. The superseded paragraph is quoted and retracted rather
        than deleted, because it is the reasoning a future reader is most likely to try to
        restore:

            RETRACTED: "A DECLINED NDA STILL BLOCKS. It counts toward the total and not toward
            the signed count, so the party exists and has not signed. If a party is genuinely
            out of the process the NDA record is DELETED, not left Declined - which is stated
            in the Declined step of NDA_Path_Disposition."

        WHY IT WAS WRONG: it made Declined a state with NO USER-CLEARABLE EXIT. A declined NDA
        blocked every forward stage from NDA onward forever, and the only remedy this file and
        lwc/ndaMarkDeclined both prescribed was to DELETE the record - on an object every
        permission set in this repo treats as an audit artefact, and which no disposition
        persona could delete anyway (allowDelete=false, and D20 keeps it false deliberately: a
        declined NDA IS the evidence of a buyer or broker who refused to sign).

        WHAT ACTUALLY CHANGED, AND WHERE: nothing here. The fix is arithmetic and it lives in
        the COUNTER. NDA_Signed_Rollup's Is_Row_Signed decision gained a third outcome that
        counts a Declined row toward NEITHER counter, so a declined party is neither
        outstanding nor signed. THE EXCLUSION COULD NOT HAVE BEEN PUT IN THIS RULE: the formula
        below sees two Numbers on the parent and has no access to child rows at all -
        NDA__c.Disposition__c is a Lookup, not Master-Detail, so there is no roll-up summary
        available and a validation rule cannot count children. The counter is the only place
        the distinction is expressible, so this was a determination rather than a preference.

        ⚠ TWO CONSEQUENCES OF THE NEW ARITHMETIC, BOTH INTENDED AND BOTH VISIBLE ONLY HERE:
        a disposition whose ONLY NDA is Declined now records NDA_Count__c = 0, and the first
        clause below STILL BLOCKS IT - which is precisely why that clause is not an oversight.
        And a disposition where the buyer declined but the introducing broker signed now PASSES:
        this gate governs the DISPOSITION's stage, and a party who declined "goes no further"
        (Part 2 line 231) while the disposition itself may still proceed with another buyer.

        ⚠ THE DEPLOY ORDER BELOW BECOMES SHARPER, NOT LOOSER. If this rule is deployed while
        the OLD version of NDA_Signed_Rollup is still active, Declined rows keep inflating
        NDA_Count__c and the gate keeps blocking - fail-closed, so it is survivable, but the
        flow must land first or the D20 fix is simply not in effect.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. The NDA_Signed_Rollup flow MUST be deployed BEFORE this
        rule. Deploying the rule first leaves both counters at 0 or null with nothing able to
        set them, so NO off-market disposition could advance past the NDA stage at all. Same
        lesson as Tranche 2's flow-before-validation-rule ordering.

        🔴 THE FIRING SURFACE CLAIM HAS NOW EXPIRED - RETRACTED 2026-08-09 BY TRANCHE 3C, AND
        THE FORMULA BELOW DID NOT CHANGE. The paragraph that stood here named this exact change
        as the moment its claim would expire, so it is quoted and retracted rather than deleted:

            RETRACTED: "FIRING SURFACE. As of this tranche Disposition_Stage__c is still written
            by nothing but user edits - the Path, the Details section and inline edit - so the
            equivalent claim in Wire_Complete_Before_Completed's comment remains TRUE and was
            deliberately not touched here. That changes in Tranche 3C, when
            ContractExecutionService becomes the first machine writer of the field (writing
            Closing, which IS in the list below); whoever makes that change must make its write
            fail-soft and must correct the claim in BOTH files then."

        WHAT REPLACED IT: DISPOSITION_STAGE__C NOW HAS TWO WRITERS. (1) User edits, as before:
        the Path, the Details section and inline edit. (2) ContractExecutionService's disposition
        arm, advanceDispositionsToClosing, which writes Disposition_Stage__c = 'Closing' when a
        sell-side PSA reaches Executed on the related Contract Review. It is the first machine
        writer of this field in the application. Both obligations that paragraph imposed have
        been met: the machine write IS fail-soft, and the sibling claim in
        Wire_Complete_Before_Completed was corrected in the same change as this one.

        🔴 THE CONSEQUENCE IS SHARPER HERE THAN IN THE SIBLING RULE: THIS RULE CAN NOW FIRE
        AGAINST A WRITE NO HUMAN MADE. 'Closing' is in the OR list below, so an automated move
        into Closing is a FORWARD move and is gated exactly like a manual one. That is correct
        and must stay: an executed PSA does not entitle an off-market sale to skip the release
        gate. What happens when it fires:
        (a) the PSA execution itself PROCEEDS. The arm's write is
            Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE), so allOrNone = false means this
            rule's rejection cannot roll back the Contract Review's Executed status, the parent
            stamp or the notifications;
        (b) the stage move is REFUSED. The disposition stays at the stage it was already on;
        (c) the record is therefore left with an EXECUTED Contract Review and a stage that did
            not advance.
        That end state is VISIBLE, NOT SILENT: both records are on screen and they plainly
        disagree, and any user can advance the stage by hand once every non-Declined NDA reads
        Signed. Do not "repair" it by relaxing this gate, and do not bypass validation on the
        Apex write.

        ⚠ NOTE FOR ANYONE READING THE ARM'S RESULTS: the DML results are deliberately not
        inspected there, so a block raises no error and writes no log. This rule's own error
        message is the only human-readable explanation of the refusal, and it renders only to a
        user who later attempts the move by hand.

        BLAST RADIUS - for the developer and testing agents. Any existing test, seed script or
        fixture that MOVES an Off_Market disposition to Disposition Offer, LOI, PSA, Closing or
        Completed will now need a signed NDA on it first. On-market rows are unaffected.
    -->
    <fullName>All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Off-market only: blocks every forward stage from NDA onward (Disposition Offer, LOI, PSA, Closing, Completed) until every NDA on this disposition that was not Declined is Signed. See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    RecordType.DeveloperName = &apos;Off_Market&apos;,
    ISCHANGED(Disposition_Stage__c),
    OR(
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Disposition Offer&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;LOI&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;PSA&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Closing&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Completed&apos;)
    ),
    OR(
        BLANKVALUE(NDA_Count__c, 0) = 0,
        BLANKVALUE(Signed_NDA_Count__c, 0) &lt; BLANKVALUE(NDA_Count__c, 0)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Disposition_Stage__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Every NDA on this disposition must be signed before information is released. Add the buyer&apos;s NDA (and the introducing broker&apos;s, if there is one) and mark each one Signed before advancing.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
